== Geology and seismology ==

The geology of Burawa reflects the ancient {{w|tectonics|tectonic}} history of [[Southwestern Kaftia]]. The [[Great Kaftian Mountain Range]] is the product of a {{w|continental collision}} approximately 350–400 million years ago. The resulting {{w|orogeny|orogen}} was once significantly taller, but hundreds of millions of years of {{w|erosion}} have reduced it to its present subdued profile.

=== Geological zones ===

The southern coastal lowlands constitute a coastal {{w|sedimentary rock|sedimentary}} zone, underlain by sedimentary deposits including significant {{w|hydrocarbon}} reserves. The [[Central Burawa]] and [[Waaq Region]] constitute a highland {{w|crystalline rock|crystalline}} zone, underlain by ancient crystalline rocks including exposed mineral veins. The [[Great Kaftian Mountain Range]] itself consists of {{w|metamorphic rock}}s from the ancient orogeny.

=== Seismicity ===

Unlike the broader [[Southwestern Kaftia]] region, which is geologically stable, Burawa experiences minor {{w|seismicity|seismic activity}} associated with the [[Great Kaftian Mountain Range]]. The mountain range, though ancient, retains residual tectonic stresses that occasionally produce small {{w|earthquake}}s.

Minor earthquakes ({{w|Richter magnitude scale|magnitude}} 2–4) occur several times per year in the highland regions. Seismic activity is concentrated along the mountain range, particularly in the [[Waaq Region]] and the border areas with [[Kushish]] and [[Kwalib]]. The seismic hazard is considered low, and no significant earthquake has caused major damage in recorded history.

== Natural resources ==

=== Minerals ===

The [[Great Kaftian Mountain Range]] contains exposed mineral veins deposited during the original {{w|orogeny}}. {{w|Iron ore}} is found throughout the [[Waaq Region]] and [[Central Burawa]], historically forming the basis of Burawi {{w|metallurgy}}. Significant deposits of {{w|copper}} exist in the highland zones, with {{w|tin}} found in association with copper deposits.

=== Hydrocarbons ===

The southern [[Mesogean Sea|Mesogean]] coast possesses significant reserves of {{w|petroleum}} and {{w|natural gas}} in offshore and near-shore formations. These reserves, concentrated off the [[Central Coast]] and [[Iskhal Megalopolis]] regions, are a major component of Burawa's modern economy.

=== Fisheries ===

Both the [[Lake Haro|Lake Haro System]] and the [[Mesogean Sea]] coast support productive {{w|fishery|fisheries}}. The Lake Haro System contains {{w|endemism|endemic}} {{w|cichlid}} species, while the Mesogean coastal waters yield {{w|tuna}}, {{w|mackerel}}, and {{w|sardine}}s.

